  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 208 PM MDT WED OCT 21 2026\nLow pressure will stay southeast of the region for the weekend, \nallowing a short-lived ridge of high pressure to build in and\nbring dry conditions and a slight warming trend through Sunday.\nTemperatures will climb to about 5-10 degrees above normal for \nSunday and Monday, with cooler and wetter conditions returning \nthanks to a Gulf of Alaska low pressure system moving inland \nfrom the northeastern Pacific. Lingering forecast uncertainty \nexists for the timing and track of this low pressure system, \nwith disagreement present in ensemble solutions and between \ndeterministic models. Current forecast shows this cut off low \nbringing much cooler, below normal temperatures and a 30-50% \nchance of precipitation over higher terrain from Tuesday to late\nWednesday. Snow levels will likely range from 5500-6500 feet, \ndepending on the track of the low pressure, with light mountain \nsnow accumulation by early Thursday.",
